{# Pandoc HTML template for slide decks. Shares head, styling and client-side
   behavior with html-template.html.j2; adds slide layout and present mode.
   Pair it with slide-sections.lua, which groups the body into .slide sections. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
{# Three levels, narrowest first: a document's own `lang:`, then the package
   or config-wide `lang:` baked in here at generation time, then `en`. The
   attribute is never omitted -- an unset language is a WCAG 2.1 failure
   (3.1.1), and both templates hardcoded `en` before this, so a project that
   sets nothing renders exactly as it did.

   `dir` is front matter only and emitted only when asked. A package's `dir:`
   is already its output subdirectory, so there is no config-level spelling to
   give it, and browsers infer `ltr` anyway -- a wrong direction is worse than
   an absent one. #}
<html lang="$if(lang)$$lang$$else${{ lang }}$endif$"$if(dir)$ dir="$dir$"$endif$>
<head>
{% include '_page-head.html.j2' %}
  <style>
{% include '_page-style.css.j2' %}

{% include '_slide-style.css.j2' %}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container deck">
{% include '_slide-body.html.j2' %}
  </div>

{% include '_page-scripts.html.j2' %}
{% include '_slide-scripts.html.j2' %}
</body>
</html>
